  "improvements": [
    "Two reviewed current-code writers read the same synthetic history. After the newer writer added a record, the stale writer silently removed it. The complete predecessor and reproduction are retained without executing archived code.",
    "The four owned history banks (history, buybacks, full auction history and asset prices) now require a complete validated read with its quoted S3 ETag before replacement. Existing keys use IfMatch; explicit missing-key initialization uses IfNoneMatch.",
    "A condition is consumed before each write, including a failed or ambiguous put. Another write requires a fresh read and merge. No automatic blind retry is introduced.",
    "A reread invalidates its prior condition before acquisition; denied/corrupt/malformed reads cannot retain obsolete write authority. Each handler invocation clears prior warm-container conditions.",
    "Existing-bank races, racing initializers, missing/malformed versions, repeated writes and ambiguous failures preserve the winner. Primary handler conflicts stop before public output. Secondary loader conflicts preserve their newer bank and surface the conflict.",
    "The synthetic object store now produces stable gzip bytes for unchanged documents, so its ETag represents a stable stored version. Existing full-history tests use real synthetic storage reads instead of replacing the reader and bypassing version checks.",
    "All existing source requests, read keys, output families, resources and schedules remain unchanged. The source-reference registry is rebuilt for changed native line numbers."
  ],
